es. They continued to fight through the Normandy Campaign and played a key role in the Battle of Caen and the liberation of Falaise. Later the division became part of the First Canadian Army and was involved in the clearing of the French channel ports and the following Battle of Boulogne. In October 1944 the division fought in the Battle of the Scheldt in Belgium, where they earned the nickname “Water Rats” in recognition of the poor terrain conditions they were forced to fight in. After that they kept fighting in France and were involved in the liberation of Boulogne-sur-Mer and Calais. After the war the 3rd served as part of the Canadian Army Occupation Force in Germany, until 1946 when it was sent back to Canada where the division was disbanded shortly after. "},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSpawnedInHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDrawnFromDeck"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Guard","EHelpBubbleTypes::Salvage"],"hasGuard":true,"hasSalvage":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'explosion_concrete_medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/explosion_concrete_medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_canadian_soldier_2.t_canadian_soldier_2","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/3rd_CANADIAN_DIVISION.3rd_CANADIAN_DIVISION","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":383.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_3rd_canadian_division_photo","SourceString":"Men of the 3rd Canadian Division moving through a French village, Juno Beach sector, Normandy, France, 6 June 1944.","LocalizedString":"Men of the 3rd Canadian Division 